{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_comment": "Six-step journey for the Gas Pipe Sizing Workbook store screenshots, replayed by scripts/media-capture.mjs and framed by scripts/store-kit.py. Every coordinate was measured from the live view hierarchy (uiautomator dump) of the signed release build on the Medium_Phone AVD at 1080x2400 / 420dpi, not guessed.",
  "_why_the_waits": "Each step is executed back to back with no settling time, and the runner waits only one second after launching the app. Compose needs longer than that to draw the form, and needs a moment between focusing a field and receiving text, or the entry lands in the wrong field or is dropped entirely. The waits below are load-bearing, not padding: without the leading one the material field silently stays empty.",
  "_preconditions": [
    "Target the release build. The debug variant carries a .debug applicationId suffix, so capturing it would photograph a package that never ships: ./gradlew :app:assembleRelease && adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk",
    "Clear the stored case first, or the first shot inherits the previous run's entries and every 'text' step appends to them: adb shell pm clear com.gexetr.pipesizing",
    "Disable the soft keyboard. Its autocorrect rewrites typed values ('psig' became 'Paige' and '100' became '100y40v4 5'), and it scrolls the form as fields are focused, which moves the coordinates this file depends on. It also has no business appearing in a store screenshot: adb shell ime list -s, then adb shell ime disable <id> for each. Disabling races with the IME service restarting, so retry until adb shell ime list -s prints nothing.",
    "Screens are captured at 1080x2400, so the phone assets are framed from a 2400px-tall source rather than 1920.",
    "After capturing, confirm the journey worked rather than trusting the PNGs: dump the view hierarchy and check the final screen still reads 'Case: Schedule 40 steel at 0.5 psig', '100.00 MBH required', '60.00 ft total run' and 'Compared capacity: 120.00 MBH'. Every value typed above feeds that result, so it is a whole-journey checksum - a keyboard that rewrote one field shows up here even though each individual tap appeared to succeed."
  ],
